TLS keying material exporters allow additional keying material to be
derived from existing TLS channel. This exported keying material can then
be used for a variety of purposes.

- Changes in the patch are made on to of crypto layer and that's reason why
they should work for both crypto backends (openssl/polarssl)

- TLS_FINAL Plugin was called in key_method_2_read() before server_random
was generated for the TLS server end-point and that's the reason why it's
called at 2 places now. key_method_2_read() for server and
key_method_2_write() for client.

Use cases:

1) Authentication of upper layer (like Kerberos etc)

2) Authentication of VPN's TLS channel using QRCODE and device such as
smartphone.

(Instead of user/pass dialog TLS VPN client could show QRCODE based on
Keying Material Derivate)

